Thanks @duolahypercho — you're right on both counts, and good catch.

**On the incomplete scope:** correct, `captureNative()` in `catalog.mjs` (both the normal path and the `--bundled` fallback) and the model-catalog probe in `doctor.mjs` all called `execFileSync(<binary>, ...)` directly with no `shell: true`. So after `codexIsAuthenticated()` started succeeding via `codex.cmd`, those paths would still throw `ENOENT` and fail to capture/recheck native models. Fixed in 5b10371.

**On the stale PR description:** also correct, and my mistake. The "catalog already handles `.cmd`" line came from a local working copy that had a `catalog.execCodex()` helper — which does **not** exist in `main`. I should have verified against the base branch before writing that; I've corrected it below. Apologies for the noise.

## What changed (5b10371)

Centralized the Windows `.cmd` handling instead of duplicating it per call site. New helper in `codex-binary.mjs`:

```js
export function runCodex(args, options = {}) {
  const binary = requireCodexBinary();
  const merged = { ...options };
  if (
    process.platform === "win32" &&
    binary.toLowerCase().endsWith(".cmd") &&
    merged.shell === undefined
  ) {
    merged.shell = true;
  }
  return execFileSync(binary, args, merged);
}
```

Every codex invocation now goes through it:
- `codexIsAuthenticated()` → `runCodex(["login","status"], …)`
- `catalog.captureNative()` → both paths → `runCodex(["debug","models", …], …)`
- `doctor.mjs` catalog probe → `runCodex(["debug","models"], …)`

Callers can still force a behavior by passing `options.shell` explicitly (opt-out), and macOS/Linux are unaffected (the `.cmd` branch is guarded by `process.platform === "win32"`).

## Verification

Reproduced on the same live Windows + npm `codex.cmd` + ChatGPT auth setup:
- `codexIsAuthenticated()` → `true`
- `captureNative()` path (`runCodex(["debug","models","--bundled"], …)`) → captures **8 native models** (was `ENOENT`)
- full `node src/catalog.mjs` → `{ native_models: 7, openai_authenticated: true, models: 9 }`
- `npm test` → 193 pass / 0 fail / 2 skipped (unchanged)
- `npm run check` → passed

Diff is now 3 files (+43/−20). Ready for another look when you have a moment.

Thanks for the detailed writeup — the diagnosis is correct and I want this in. Centralizing on `runCodex()` so `catalog.mjs` and `doctor.mjs` get the same treatment was the right call; both had the identical latent bug.

One blocking issue before merge.

### `shell: true` does not quote the command, so paths with spaces break

`runCodex()` passes `binary` to `execFileSync` unquoted with `shell: true`. Node builds the shell command by concatenating file and args without quoting, so a path like `C:\Users\John Smith\AppData\Roaming\npm\codex.cmd` splits into two tokens and fails. Windows usernames with spaces are common enough that this will bite people.

Reproduced locally (same unquoted-concatenation path on POSIX, easier to demo):

```
no-shell:     ok login status
shell:true:   FAILED — /bin/sh: /…/dir: No such file or directory
quoted+shell: ok login status
```

This matters more than it did before the PR, because `captureNative()` and the doctor `debug models` call now route through `runCodex` too — previously they ran without a shell and handled spaces fine.

Suggested fix:

```js
export function runCodex(args, options = {}) {
  const binary = requireCodexBinary();
  const merged = { ...options };
  const needsShell =
    process.platform === "win32" && /\.(cmd|bat)$/i.test(binary);
  if (needsShell && merged.shell === undefined) merged.shell = true;
  // shell:true does not quote the command, so a path with spaces
  // (e.g. C:\Users\John Smith\...) would split into two tokens.
  return execFileSync(merged.shell ? `"${binary}"` : binary, args, merged);
}
```

`cmd.exe /d /s /c` strips the outer quotes correctly, so this is safe on Windows and a no-op elsewhere.

Worth widening the extension check to `.bat` while you're in there, and matching it in `findCodexBinary()`'s preference list.

### Minor

The description says `catalog.execCodex()` already handled `.cmd` with `shell: true` — there's no `execCodex` and no `shell: true` anywhere in `src/` on `main`. Doesn't change anything about the patch, just noting it so the rationale in the commit history stays accurate.

### Verification on my side

- Test suite on your branch: 173 pass / 8 fail — **identical failure set to baseline `f2bbe96`**, so no regression from this change. The 8 are pre-existing and unrelated (Kimi OAuth, provider usage, quota adapters).
- CI hasn't actually run yet — it's sitting at `action_required` pending maintainer approval. I'll approve the run so the Windows leg of the matrix executes against the updated patch.

No unit test needed — I agree mocking `node:child_process` from ESM isn't worth restructuring the module for on a bugfix this size.

Push the quoting fix and I'll merge.

Pushed the quoting fix and the `.bat` widening in 53f7913. Thanks for the reproduce — confirmed it independently before patching.

## Verification (Windows)

Isolated the pure quoting behavior with a minimal `.cmd`/`.bat` in a spaced path (`C:\Users\krist\AppData\Local\Temp\dir with space\`):

| mode | result |
| --- | --- |
| `no-shell` | `EINVAL` (Node can't spawn `.cmd` at all) |
| `shell:true` unquoted | `FAILED` — path splits at the space: `'C:\...\dir' is not recognized` |
| `shell:true` quoted | `OK: "ran HELLO"` |

And against the real (space-less) `codex.cmd`:
- `codexIsAuthenticated()` → `true`
- `captureNative()` path → 8 native models
- `npm test` → 193 pass / 0 fail / 2 skipped (unchanged)
- `npm run check` → passed

## Changes (53f7913)

```js
export function runCodex(args, options = {}) {
  const binary = requireCodexBinary();
  const merged = { ...options };
  const needsShell =
    process.platform === "win32" && /\.(cmd|bat)$/i.test(binary);
  if (needsShell && merged.shell === undefined) {
    merged.shell = true;
  }
  // With shell:true, Node concatenates file+args without quoting, so a path
  // containing spaces (e.g. C:\Users\John Smith\...) would split into two
  // tokens and fail. Quote the command; cmd.exe /d /s /c strips the outer
  // quotes correctly, and this branch is Windows-only.
  return execFileSync(merged.shell ? `"${binary}"` : binary, args, merged);
}
```

- Widened the shim check from `.cmd` to `/\.(cmd|bat)$/i` in both `runCodex()` and `findCodexBinary()`'s preference list, since `.bat` has the identical spawn limitation.
- `findCodexBinary()` now prefers `/\.(cmd|bat)$/i` before `.exe` before the extensionless first entry.

## On the minor note

Agreed on the stale `execCodex`/`shell: true` rationale — there is no `execCodex` and no `shell: true` anywhere in `src/` on `main`. That line in the original commit message came from a local working copy that diverged from base; it's inaccurate and I shouldn't have written it. The later commits describe the actual change correctly (centralizing on `runCodex()`), and nothing in the patch depends on that rationale. Happy to reword the first commit message if you'd prefer the history clean — just say the word.

